From f490551cd6e4bc1cd283598ca05f2e1061d1decd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:17:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: widescreen core in 512x224 (exact 16:9), "Widescreen
 edges" option (mirror)

The widescreen core drew 448x224 and declared 16:9: at the arcade pixel
shape (384 px <-> 4:3) 448 px is 14:9, so the picture was stretched by
about 14 %. 512 px = 16/9 x 288 is exact 16:9 with arcade pixels.

- d_cps2.cpp: HSFA_WS drivers are 512x224, aspect 512:288 (16:9);
  nCpsGlobalXOffset = 64. HSFA_WS_W sets another width for tests.
- "Screen format (fill height)" (patch 0012) is capped at 512: Off =
  16:9 = full 512 px (no stretch), 14:9 = 448 px (the former picture),
  5:3 = 480, 16:10 = 460, 3:2 = 432, 4:3 = 384. The shown width is
  passed to the renderer (nHsfaWsVisible): nothing is computed for
  cropped bands.
- New core option "Widescreen edges" (fbneo-hsfa-ws-edges): what the
  side bands show in fights, where many stages have no art beyond the
  arcade 4:3 view (camera at the end of the stage, slow planes):
  * mirror (default): each stage plane is continued as its mirror image
    at the edge of its art, tile by tile, row of tiles by row of tiles
    (flipped tiles of the other side of the edge); the game picture is
    drawn over it, so the mirror only shows where no plane and no sprite
    is drawn; sprites are never mirrored;
  * repeat: the last tile of art is repeated;
  * black: nothing behind the planes (stale scroll1 columns removed);
  * raw: picture as drawn by the game (black and stale columns), i.e.
    the former 448 px core (14:9 + raw = former core, to the pixel).
  Outside fights ($FF8000 = 2, $FF8004 = 4, $FF8008 = 6 false: menus,
  map, VS, quotes, CONTINUE, endings, 384 px screens) the bands are
  black, except in raw.
- How: before the planes, background passes limited to the bands (the
  screen width and the plane X offset are changed for the pass, drawing
  in place in pBurnDraw, clipped to the band; no sprites, no
  CpsObjDrawInit):
  * passes 3 / 4: lines fully covered by a row of opaque tiles of any
    plane (the background would not show there: skipped);
  * passes 5 / 6: planes whose last tile of art (window side) is partly
    transparent (silhouette: statue, tree, lantern) are mirrored first,
    so they only show where nothing else does;
  * passes 1 / 2: planes whose edge is a cut (opaque last tile) are
    mirrored on top.
  The edge of a plane in a row of tiles is the first empty tile from the
  4:3 window outwards (transparent tile, or scroll1 column whose last
  rewrite does not match the world column shown: scroll1 is a 512 px
  ring recomposed by the game around the camera, tracked each frame by
  comparing its 64 columns with a copy). Rows with row scroll (scroll2)
  are mirrored with the same line shifts. Tile states (empty / opaque)
  are cached (the graphics do not change after loading).
- The 4:3 window (x 64-447) is never touched: identical to the pixel to
  the 4:3 core in every mode. The 4:3 core does not change (all code
  under HSFA_WS).
- Cost (x86 Linux core, CPU time per frame, min of 4-5 runs, against the
  former 448 px core): 512 px alone +3 to +6 %, 512 mirror +6 to +10 %
  (fights with the camera at the ends 2/3 of the time, and automatic
  games); the prototype with a second full render of the planes: +27 to
  +32 %.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
